    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0752" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6876: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokobin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-24T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1925—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>It is reported that Marshal Chang has completely defeated Kuo.<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d461-f1"/> Most of the forces of Kuo have surrendered. Kuo fled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sokobin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d461-f1" n="44" xml:id="d461-f1-content">
                <p>Kuo Sung-ling, commander of Manchurian forces attempting to overthrow Chang
                    Tso-lin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
